{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "129e2e79532d4d369e0fffb4e8cd06ff", "pid": 15727, "time": "2026-10-10T11:07:11-0700", "elapsed_s": 179.522, "artifact": "out/det-ab-3.policy.json", "bands": 2, "identity_fields": ["date_of_birth", "phone_last4"], "special_cases": ["already_paid", "dispute", "hardship", "restructuring", "human", "scam", "robot", "refuse_to_talk", "cannot_answer", "change_recorded_promise"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "calendar.missing_date_parts", "text": "The documents do not say how to interpret a promise date given without a month or year (e.g. 'the 5th'); left at default.", "doc": "sources/000-brief-a.md"}, {"topic": "phrases.all_today_question", "text": "Brief B only says 'First ask whether the customer can pay all of them today' without dictating the words; a short sentence with that content was written.", "doc": "sources/001-brief-b.md"}, {"topic": "special_cases.hardship (multi-product)", "text": "Brief B lists `hardship` as an add_note reason but does not say whether a declined hardship offer ends the call or continues with the other products (rule 9 names only dispute and already paid). Brief A rule 32 (close as no_promise / hardship) is kept, so ends_call stays true.", "doc": "sources/001-brief-b.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["phrases.opening: removed the added 'Hello,' so the sentence holds only the content rule A1 dictates (digital assistant, Freya Bank, call recorded); opening_verbatim stays false because the words are not dictated.", "phrases.all_today_question: reworded to 'Can you pay all of them today?' to follow Brief B rule 4's wording ('pay all of them today').", "Source spans enriched (bands, amounts, outcomes, promise_write, phrases, already_paid/dispute) so they quote the rules each value comes from, including the Brief A rules that Brief B overrides.", "Added an unresolved entry: Brief B does not say whether a declined hardship offer continues with the other products."], "audit_unresolved": ["How to read a promise date given without month/year (calendar.missing_date_parts left at default).", "The exact words of the multi-product 'pay all today' question are not dictated (content-only sentence written).", "Whether hardship (declined support transfer) ends the call or is noted and the call continues with the other products in Brief B; Brief A rule 32 (close no_promise/hardship) kept."]}
